# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (Codex K03-READ-FIELD-CLOSURE-20261008-31): an explicit anchor in copied code.  Outer's code
# holds `m: merge: Model`, whose use of x is anchored at the unit -- in the walked frame SELF, the unit of the running
# code.  o copies Outer with that code; o's copy of the unit holds what Outer's code uses -- Model and, through
# Model's code, x -- and not u: a frame holding the unit itself would copy the unit whole.  Exit 7.
int: x 3
int: u 4
Model:
    int: k 0
    k: x
end: Model
Outer:
    int: j 0
    m: merge: Model
end: Outer
o: merge: Outer
int: ok 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
